Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Locusts Boil the Copper Kettle
- Story & Context: When a three-day cloud of migratory locusts invaded the scrap depot at Bir Lahmar, soundman Tariq refused to let the insects devour the calfskin heads of his four scavenged symphonic timpani, choosing instead to pummel the copper bowls at maximum velocity to shake them free. The resulting syncopated sub-bass thud, paired with a blisteringly cheerful chord progression hammered out on an overheating Roland Juno-60 by Amina, turned the swarm's chaotic rattling into an accidental, triumphant dancehall rhythm that had three hundred panicked merchants dancing atop their shipping containers. Over the deafening clatter of wing-beats and forty-hertz kettle booms, General Papaya snatched the CB radio microphone and shouted the refrain that birthed a movement: "Mash up di sand-cloud, beat di kettle till di brass sweat gold!" The recorded field cassette, coated in bug dust and motor oil, became the blueprint for the entire Erg Chebbi sound.
