Track 2: Amina's Chrysalis at Bir Zreig
- Story & Context: In the scorched aluminum fuselage of a downed twin-engine transport plane near the salt well of Bir Zreig, Amina spent four sleepless days rewiring the corroded filter board of an unearthed Korg Mono/Poly, her fingers stained indigo with battery acid and henna. The heat inside the metal hull reached fifty degrees Celsius, causing the synthesizer's voice oscillators to drift into wild, ecstatic microtonal intervals that mirrored the high-pitched drone of desert cicadas burying into the clay. When caravan drivers banged on the fuselage demanding she shut down her screeching solar generator, she threw open the emergency hatch and answered with a blinding major-key dancehall progression underpinned by Tariq's booming, chromatic timpani pedal-slides. Weeping through the laughter of dehydration, she yelled into the sand, "I tear off di old skin and step out shining like a solar plate!" That night, no one in Bir Zreig slept; they danced until their sandals split.
