Track 3: Which Way Did the Brood Migrate?
- Story & Context: Myth holds that during the legendary solar eclipse of the Great Erg, the migratory scarabs emerged from the dunes and marched directly toward the Saffron Scarab Syndicate’s mega-rig, drawn by the subterranean 98-BPM rumble of forty-hertz copper pitch glides. For twelve continuous hours, the caravan played without pause, feeding dry hibiscus tea and sweet dates to the exhausted timpanists while hundreds of nomads danced shoulder-to-shoulder with the scurrying carapaces. When the sun broke through the shadow, border guards discovered the desert empty except for five hundred yards of discarded beetle shells arranged in identical, symmetrical rows resembling the white and black keys of a grand clavinet. Still echoing from the dunes was the lingering, wind-carried vocal refrain that every caravan child now sings at dawn: "Follow di heavy kettle drop until di sun crack open wide!"
